      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If they become defensive, gently pivot the conversation back to observable professional impact. A good strategy is to use \"I\" statements, like, \"I understand scheduling challenges exist, but my concern is how the delays affect the team's ability to move forward promptly.\" Reiterate that the discussion is about process improvement, not personal conduct. Keeping your tone calm and focused strictly on meeting outcomes, like \"What support do you need to ensure you can be present for the start of these vital syncs?\" will keep it professional.",
